WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.367
-Welcome back!
We are talking to the one,

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:04.133
the only John Goodman
right here!

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:06.634
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:08.534
Hopefully, you can feel
the love.

00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:11.367
Hopefully you can feel the love
through Zoom.

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:15.000
You star in not only one but two
TV shows right now.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.033
You have "The Conners"
over at ABC,

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:19.334
which airs Wednesdays at 9:00.

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:20.968
How is everything over there
at "The Conners"?

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:23.000
-Everything is great.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.868
One of my daughters,
Lecy Goranson,

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:28.434
who plays Becky in the show
has written the script

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:29.534
that we're going to do
next week,

00:00:29.534 --> 00:00:31.033
so that's going to be great.

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:34.601
It's pretty tight
and we have a lot of fun.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:37.901
-Yeah, isn't that cool
to see the way it just --

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:40.100
the opportunities you get,
you know, because you --

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.734
gosh, she was a child when
she first started on the show.

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:45.434
-Yeah, she's still childish.

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:46.968
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:49.200
-Yeah, I think you have to
be to be in this business,

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.534
right, yeah.

00:00:50.534 --> 00:00:52.701
And then let's talk about
"The Righteous Gemstones".

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:55.501
This is its second season
on HBO.

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:57.901
Danny McBride, really funny guy.

00:00:57.901 --> 00:00:59.400
What is happening this season?

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.767
-Uh, they're --

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:03.968
they're trying to merge with
another mega church.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:06.067
-Yeah.

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:09.300
-And I have an old friend who
shows up from my days

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.534
when I was
a professional wrestler,

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:14.367
which I didn't know about,
but it's great to find out.

00:01:14.367 --> 00:01:16.334
-[ Laughs ] I love that.

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:17.667
-I get kind of a girlfriend,

00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:19.100
but there's all kinds of stuff
happening.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.534
-Yeah, I know, the first episode
this season,

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:26.033
your character gets into
a fight in a parking lot.

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:28.701
But then I heard that you got
injured doing that fight.

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:31.868
Is that true?
-I was trying to be stunt boy.

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:33.300
-Yeah.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.367
-I'm not 69 years old, I'm 23,

00:01:36.367 --> 00:01:38.133
and I'll do this all night
if I have to.

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:40.801
I'll prove --
I'll prove my worth.

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:43.934
But, yeah, it was --
it was late in the night

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:47.868
and I was too tired to actually
be doing this stuff,

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:51.667
so I slipped in the gravel and
flew headfirst

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:53.834
into the back of a truck.

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:55.901
And you know that expression,
you get your bell rung.

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:58.000
That's the loudest thing I have
ever heard in my life

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.734
was the back of that truck
hitting my head.

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:02.100
-Wow.
-But everything turned out okay.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:05.400
-Yeah. Did you have to go
to the hospital?

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:06.934
-Yeah, I went to the hospital.

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:08.133
They gave me a bunch of screens.

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:10.501
They couldn't tell if I've got
a concussion,

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:13.334
or had a concussion,
so I guess I'm okay.

00:02:13.334 --> 00:02:14.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.300
-Did they use that take?

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.367
-They couldn't tell if I had
a concussion,

00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:20.400
so I guess I'm okay.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:24.601
-That is a professional --

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:26.701
a professional doing
professional comedy,

00:02:26.701 --> 00:02:27.901
ladies and gentlemen.

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:29.701
That's exactly what that is.

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:32.033
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:34.634
Here is John Goodman in
"The Righteous Gemstones".

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:36.834
Take a look at this. [ Laughs ]

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:37.868
-What do you want?

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:40.467
-I just want to see
an old friend.

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:43.701
The older I get, the more
sentimental I'm leaning.

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:45.400
Nostalgic.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.467
And I can't help but thinking
about when you and I

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.167
worked together.

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:50.801
-You want money.

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:53.200
You're going to try to blackmail
me, sell the story.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.000
Let's not waste time here.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.400
-Why all nervous, Eli?

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.567
Why you being all...[ Laughs ]
weird.

00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:01.734
-You following me, that's weird.

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:03.367
Whatever it is you are trying to
pull here,

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:04.968
I don't got time for it.

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:06.634
-Come on, Eli.

00:03:06.634 --> 00:03:08.167
Can't old friends reconnect?

00:03:08.167 --> 00:03:10.467
Oh, man.

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:11.534
♪♪

00:03:11.534 --> 00:03:13.934
-I-I'm busy.

00:03:13.934 --> 00:03:15.734
Take care.

00:03:16.167 --> 00:03:18.734
-Come on.
That's a stud right there.

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:19.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:21.400
That's John Goodman, everybody!

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.701
"The Righteous Gemstones"
airs Sundays at 10:00 PM

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:25.801
on HBO.

